    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Congruent groups: a, d, e, g; b, f, l; c, h; j, k. Part i has no congruent partner in the list.\n\nGroup parabolas with the same absolute value of the coefficient of $x^2$.",
      "worked": "A translation changes the position of a parabola without changing its shape. Reflection in the $x$-axis changes the sign of its quadratic coefficient. Thus parabolas with equal $|a|$ in $y=ax^2+bx+c$ are congruent under the permitted transformations.\n\nFor a, d, e and g, $|a|=2$, so these four are congruent.\n\nFor b, f and l, $|a|=3$, so these three are congruent.\n\nFor c and h, $|a|=5$, so these two are congruent.\n\nFor j and k, $|a|=1$, so these two are congruent.\n\nFor i, $|a|=7$; no other listed parabola has this value.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
